# Exercises Returns & Warranty against the compose stack (`make up`): the demo Customer asks what
# their Order is eligible for and requests a return of a delivered phone, after the requests it
# refuses; Staff approve it, receive the phone and inspect it; and, standing in for the returns
# Saga with Orchestration's token, it is refunded. One RMA, from request to resolution, by hand.
# Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the token requests store tokens for
# the ones after them. Orchestration's client secret is the stack's own: run it in the `dev`
# environment, whose http-client.private.env.json holds it (the root README's "Secrets").
# It needs a delivered Order of the demo Customer's with a phone: check one out in the Storefront,
# pack its Shipment in the Admin Console, and wait about 30 seconds for the mock carrier to deliver
# it. Then set @orderId to the Order's ID, @variantId to the phone's Variant ID, and @imei to the
# IMEI entered when it was packed (GET /api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?orderId= shows them).

@returns = http://localhost:8100
@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@orderId = <the delivered Order's ID>
@variantId = <the phone's Variant ID>
@imei = <the phone's IMEI>

### The demo Customer's token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Orchestration token: the returns Saga's own identity, for the steps only it takes
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=orchestration&client_secret={{orchestrationClientSecret}}

> {% client.global.set("orchestrationToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### What each delivered line is still eligible for: the Return Period's and Warranty Window's ends, and the IMEIs and quantity free to claim
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/eligibility?orderId={{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### An IMEI not shipped on that Order: 422 serialNotShipped
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1,
 "serialNumbers": ["490154203237518"], "kind": "RETURN", "reason": "Not what I expected"}

### Two phones when one was delivered: 422 quantityExceeded, with what is available (1)
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 2,
 "serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}", "490154203237518"], "kind": "RETURN", "reason": "Both broken"}

### A return of the phone, naming its IMEI, through the gateway: 201, REQUESTED, with the Return Period and its Refund amount
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}"],
 "kind": "RETURN", "reason": "Not what I expected"}

> {% client.global.set("returnId", response.body.id); %}

### The same phone again, as a warranty claim: 422 quantityExceeded, since the return holds the only unit
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}"],
 "kind": "WARRANTY_CLAIM", "reason": "It stopped charging"}

### An Order that isn't the Customer's, or isn't delivered: 404
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "no-such-order", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "kind": "RETURN",
 "reason": "Not what I expected"}

### Without an Idempotency-Key: 400
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "kind": "RETURN",
 "reason": "Not what I expected"}

### The Customer's own RMAs, newest first, as their Returns page lists them
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Staff's RMA approval queue: requested RMAs, oldest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas?status=REQUESTED&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A rejection without a reason: 400 naming reason
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Staff approve the return, with a note: APPROVED, with its Send-back deadline and Warehouse
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "Send it to the Berlin Warehouse"}

### Deciding it again: 409 rmaAlreadyDecided
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Changed our minds"}

### The Customer reads it, with its RMA history
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Customer can't decide: 403
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Expiring it before its units arrive is the returns Saga's alone: 404 through the gateway
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/expire
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}

### Staff awaiting units, by Send-back deadline, soonest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas?status=APPROVED
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### Receiving another unit than the RMA's: 422 serialMismatch, naming it
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"serialNumbers": ["490154203237518"]}

### Staff receive the phone by its IMEI: RECEIVED
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/receive
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}"]}

### Expiring it now that its units arrived: 409 transitionRefused, so the receipt wins
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/expire
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}

### A warranty claim's outcome for a return: 422 outcomeNotForKind
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/inspect
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": "FAULT_CONFIRMED"}

### Staff inspect it: INSPECTED, ACCEPTED (REFUSED would need a note)
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/inspect
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"outcome": "ACCEPTED", "note": "Unopened, as new"}

### Closing an accepted return: 422 resolutionContradictsInspection
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"resolution": "CLOSED"}

### The returns Saga resolves it once refunded: REFUNDED, and orderFullyRefunded when the phone was the Order's only unit
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/resolve
Authorization: Bearer {{orchestrationToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"resolution": "REFUNDED", "paymentTransactionReference": "<the Refund's gateway reference>"}

### The Customer reads it, resolved, with every step in its RMA history
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
